## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates expertise in enterprise-grade multi-region secret management, policy enforcement, and operational resilience within complex GitOps architectures.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region Secrets Manager replication for high availability
- Automated KMS key rotation for enhanced security
- Least-privilege IAM roles and cross-account access patterns
- OPA-like policy enforcement gates for production safety
- Automated disaster recovery testing and rollback orchestration

## Code Example
```javascript
// CDK snippet (high level)
import * as secrets from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-secretsmanager';
import * as kms from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-kms';

const encryptionKey = new kms.Key(this, 'AppKey', {
  enableKeyRotation: true,
  removalPolicy: cdk.RemovalPolicy.RETAIN
});

const secret = new secrets.Secret(this, 'AppSecret', {
  encryptionKey,
  replicationRegions: ['us-east-1', 'eu-west-1'],
  removalPolicy: cdk.RemovalPolicy.RETAIN
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical resilience planning, cross-region deployment, and IaC-driven CI/CD integration with chaos engineering signals.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region ECS/Fargate with per-branch preview environments
- App Mesh traffic routing for sophisticated traffic management
- Route 53 latency-based routing for optimal user experience
- AWS Fault Injection Simulator as a quality gate before production promotion
- Automatic rollback criteria tied to SLO violations
- DR runbook for regional failover procedures
- Observability-driven development with p95 latency and error rate SLOs

## Code Example
```javascript
// CDK snippet for FIS experiment template (illustrative)
const fisExperiment = new CfnResource(this, 'FISExperiment', {
  type: 'AWS::FIS::ExperimentTemplate',
  properties: {
    description: 'Chaos experiment for p95 latency validation',
    targets: {
      ECSClusterTarget: {
        resourceType: 'AWS::ECS::Cluster',
        selectionMode: 'ALL',
      },
    },
    actions: {
      latencyInjection: {
        actionId: 'aws:chaos:inject:network:latency',
        parameters: {
          duration: 'PT2M',
          latencyMs: '500',
          percentage: '25',
        },
      },
    },
    stopConditions: [{
      source: 'aws:cloudwatch:metric',
      value: 'p95_latency > 200',
    }],
  },
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests real-world multi-region deployments with a focus on safe migrations, feature flags, and resilient traffic routing. It evaluates understanding of cross-region IaC, data migrations, and DR readiness.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region CDK deployments
- Backward-compatible DynamoDB migrations
- Feature flags with AppConfig
- Route 53 latency-based routing and Canary shifts
- Automated rollback and DR runbook

## Code Example

```typescript
// cdk stack sketch (TypeScript)
import * as cdk from 'aws-cdk-lib';
import { RestApi } from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-apigateway';
import { Table } from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-dynamodb';

export class ApiStack extends cdk.Stack {
  constructor(scope: cdk.App, id: string, props?: cdk.StackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);
    new RestApi(this, 'RealTimeApi');
    new Table(this, 'DataTable', {
      partitionKey: { name: 'PK', type: cdk.aws-dynamodb.AttributeType.STRING },
      sortKey: { name: 'SK', type: cdk.aws-dynamodb.AttributeType.STRING },
      // add-only migrations handled outside of this stack
    });
  }
}
```

